{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>What their end would be.</b> What will come of them in the end." "<b>For they are a generation of perversity.</b> They turn My will to anger." "<b>No faithfulness in them.</b> My rearing is not recognizable in them — for I taught them a good path and they turned aside from it." "<b>Faithfulness.</b> In the sense of ״וַיְהִי אֹמֵן״ (Esther 2) — נורריטור\"ה בְּלַעַ\"ז. Another interpretation: <b>faithfulness</b> in the sense of אֱמוּנָה, as the Targum renders. They said at Sinai 'we will do and we will hear,' yet for a fleeting hour they cancelled their pledge and made the calf (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {3 "the la'az נורריטור\"ה is Old French nourreture, 'nurturing / rearing'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:17.907471757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}